From 2ad0d43db60d84108a6d3abe5ef13fb058f21aff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emaki contributors <emaki@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:39:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] network/nm: name the activation a connection failure belongs
 to

A connection failure arrives asynchronously. A client that starts another
connection attempt on the same network could not tell a late failure of
the earlier attempt from a failure of the new one, and some failures were
reported with a stale reason or not at all.

- Network.activation names the network's current activation; with
  NetworkManager it is the D-Bus path of the active connection, new for
  every activation. While connectionFailed is emitted it names the
  activation that failed.
- NMDevice kept the reason of its last Failed state across activations,
  so an activation that ended without failing (a disconnect, a newer
  activation replacing it) was reported with an earlier activation's
  failure reason. The reason is now cleared when an activation starts
  (device state Prepare), and a failure is reported only when the device
  failed during the activation.
- Failure reasons other than the five mapped ones (IpConfigUnavailable
  when DHCP gives no address, for one) emitted nothing; they are now
  reported as ConnectionFailReason.Unknown.

Test: connectionfailure in src/network/test (BUILD_TESTING).
